.TH GENESIS-LANGUAGE 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-language \- the language faculties of the Genesis mind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBtemporal_lobe.comprehension\fR    receptive language (the Wernicke side)
\fBfrontal_lobe.generator\fR         productive language (the Broca side)
\fBtemporal_lobe.morphology\fR       shared English inflection engine
\fBtemporal_lobe.semantics\fR        compositional meaning synthesis
\fBtemporal_lobe.vocabulary\fR       context-sensitive word selection
\fBtemporal_lobe.figurative\fR       metaphor and non-literal meaning
\fBtemporal_lobe.speech\fR           Piper TTS / Vosk STT
\fBtemporal_lobe.language_latent_space\fR  machine-native text geometry
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis contains no language model and never will. Everything she
understands or says is composed endogenously: comprehension parses
speech into meaning, the generator composes meaning into speech, and
a single morphosyntax engine keeps the two sides agreeing about
English.
.SS Comprehension \(em the receptive side
.I temporal_lobe/comprehension.py
performs basic semantic parsing: speech-act identification
(question, statement, command, exclamation \(em Searle), proposition
extraction into subject-predicate-object triples, and reference
resolution (Hobbs; centering theory). Propositions feed the
discourse situation model so a "Where is Mary?" mid-story is
answered from what she just heard, not from the web.
.SS Semantics
.I temporal_lobe/semantics.py
composes the constituents comprehension supplies \(em a proposition's
subject, predicate, roles, embeddings \(em into the sense they
collectively express, on Frege's principle of compositionality. The
anterior temporal semantic-hub role: convergence of distributed
features into one coherent meaning.
.SS Generation \(em the productive side
.I frontal_lobe/generator.py
takes a Thought (semantic content + intent + emotion + metadata) and
composes it into language: grammar selects the sentence structure
for the intent, vocabulary fills the slots, voice applies rhythm,
connectors, hedging, and register. The result is composed, not
retrieved \(em never a template with slots filled.
.SS Vocabulary and morphology
.I temporal_lobe/vocabulary.py
selects words grounded in the concept network, emotional state
(cortisol shortens, dopamine enlivens), and personality (openness
abstracts, conscientiousness measures). It is context-sensitive
selection, not a thesaurus.
.I temporal_lobe/morphology.py
is the shared inflectional engine \(em comprehension deconjugates
("runs" \(-> "run"), production conjugates ("it runs"), and because
both read the same module they can never disagree about English.
.SS The machine-native latent space
.I temporal_lobe/language_latent_space.py
is her own text geometry: reversible 7-bit ASCII notation, a
deterministic hashed feature codebook, and a Sinkhorn
optimal-transport coupling between observed code distributions and
the codebook. NumPy only \(em an optimal-transport summary, not a
learned semantic map, and no pretrained anything.
.SS Voice
.I temporal_lobe/speech.py
provides Piper neural TTS (espeak-ng fallback) and Vosk speech-to-
text. Hearing itself is documented in
.BR genesis-hearing (7).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Self_World/temporal_lobe/
The language faculties and the concept network they ground in.
.TP
.I Self_World/frontal_lobe/generator.py
The productive engine.
